            "creation_time": "2020-05-01T02:45:12Z",
            "text": "Created attachment 2585\nadd lwd argument to barplot.default\n\n> barplot(1:10, lwd = .5)\n\nshould \"just work\". Current workaround is fairly awkward compared to most other base plotting methods which do accept lwd:\n\n> old = par('lwd')\n> par(lwd = .5)\n> barplot(1:10)\n> par(lwd = old)\n\nFrom a glance at the code, there's two options:\n\n 1. Pass ... to internal helper xyrect(), which then passes it to rect(), which understands lwd [the potential issue is ... is currently being passed to plot.window(); I'm not sure if there's any potential side effects]\n 2. Add lwd as an argument to barplot.default(), then to xyrect(). This will surely work, the downside I guess is that barplot.default already has 31 arguments.\n\nI have attached option 2 as a patch.\n\nPS lwd could probably be added to a few other plotting functions -- at a glance I notice the same applies to hist.default()",
